        <headline>Beach Hazards Statement issued September 24 at 5:02AM EDT until September 24 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Newport/Morehead City NC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Beach Hazards Statements, strong longshore
currents in the surf zone.

* WHERE...Bogue Banks beaches.

* WHEN...For the Beach Hazards Statement, until 8 PM EDT this
evening.

* IMPACTS...Strong longshore currents will create dangerous
swimming conditions.
</description>
        <instruction>Strong longshore currents can sweep swimmers and surfers into rip
currents, piers, jetties and other hazardous areas. In many
cases, the longshore current is strong enough to prevent swimmers
from being able to keep their feet on the bottom making it
difficult to return to shore.</instruction>
